post:
Realized That I Don't Feel Anything Anymore Hello, beautiful people of Reddit.

&amp;#x200B;

I've been going back and forth lately trying to figure out what is up with me. I have always been a bit of a procrastinator, but for most of the past year I've gotten ridiculously lazy and it annoys the hell out of me. Today I realized I don't really feel anything anymore. No happiness, no feeling of getting excited, no anger, no sadness...just pure meh 24/7. I don't like it.

&amp;#x200B;

Quick context and a bit about me:

&amp;#x200B;

Got married 3 years ago and my wife is perfect. She is hard-working, loving, honest, and gets more beautiful every day. I am truly blessed. For some reason, since we've gotten married I've gotten more lazy. My career hasn't gone how I wanted, and I've begun letting people take advantage of me in my career. I've had a job that I'm really happy about lined up for a few months, but it's taking way longer than anticipated to get a start date. I worked so hard during the year or two before we got married, worked out every day and worked on my side hustles, and I think about that time period a lot. I'd love to get back to that state of mind, because it was me at my best.

&amp;#x200B;

Lately, I work out inconsistently and I don't work out with the same intensity that I used to. I could be eating better. I definitely watch too much porn. I get very little done because I constantly get distracted by one thing or another. I've grown really tired of my ways, and all I really want is to be an incredibly hard worker. I need to get rid of being lazy and do all the things I want to do, but I haven't been able to do it.

&amp;#x200B;

I've never thought of myself as depressed before, but I'm starting to think that might be the case, I'm not sure. I'd just love to talk to some people or hear some objective perspectives, and if anyone would like to throw in their two cents, I'd be extremely grateful and would love to talk.

Are Breakups one of the leading cause of depression for men? I've heard from a friend that is taking psychology that approximately around 70-80% of men going through clinical depression was caused from a breakup. It seems so unreal, but I just wanted to understand if this fact was real. 

&amp;#x200B;

Me personally, I've been prescribed through anti-depressants just because of a breakup... I even was taken to a crisis counselor to deal with my trauma. Breakups in my opinion is just such as small thing when it comes to depression compared to people that have had abusive parents, have no friends, lonely, and not wanted. It's weird to say that breakups do turn your world upside down but in my opinion it should be as bad since there was an experience in happiness at one point...

&amp;#x200B;

Statistically speaking, if anyone knows, what is the leading cause of depression for men and women? 

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

Past mistakes are making it hard for me to move on Hello,   


&amp;#x200B;

I have made some silly mistakes in life - treated people disrespectfully physically and emotionally. I have cheated, lied, and there have been some very very drunk nights, which have been blurs and that have led to borderline sexual assault  - or made girls very uncomfortable at the least. Nothing that has ever gotten me in trouble with the law, though.  


&amp;#x200B;

Recently - this has all caught up to me. I have not done anything like what I have mentioned in the last 4 years, and life was generally okay.  


&amp;#x200B;

I'm 27 now, and now I feel like shit. I always thought I was a "good" person, that's what people told me anyway. Now I can't even look at myself without getting angry.   


&amp;#x200B;

I moved across the country and thought that a new start would help, but it's done nothing. I've brought it all with me. I've reached out to the people I may have hurt, and apologized. I got 2/3 responses from them saying "We were young, I'm glad you're doing okay" etc. No response from the 3rd. I thought reaching out and apologizing would help, because I deeply felt sorry and hold onto to so much guilt. I can't believe I did some of things I did when I was younger.   
The 3rd is married, with kids. I've made enough of a fool of myself reaching out and apologizing - 3 messages without responses. 

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

I should stop - but I hold so much guilt and really want forgiveness.   


&amp;#x200B;

Everything fun has become "What's the point" and it's ruined my relationship, and ruined how I act around people - to the point where they actually say that I've changed and I'm not the same person.   


&amp;#x200B;

Anyone new I talk to, I have this urge to tell them that "Hey, you might think I'm a good person, but I'm not - and heres why"   


&amp;#x200B;

Every day I wake up feeling more and more distant from family, friends and just life in general. Anything that happens, say a physical item breaking or something going wrong at work, I don't even get annoyed and just think "Oh yeah well I deserve that". 




I have tried to talk to a psychologist, but I have a hard time trying to put across exactly what I'm trying to say. I feel nothing is working. 




I don't know how to move on and forgive myself, or learn to be able to move on. 

&amp;#x200B;
